 "limits": [
  "Small subtasks (20 to 30 images for several); scores quantised in 2.5 to 5 point steps, so ties and rank differences are noisy",
  "Only easy OCR, numerical, translation and code items in this version; authors concede capability coverage and reasoning scenarios are limited",
  "Yes/no format gives acc ~50% to always-yes models and rewards no-bias, conflating hallucination with failure to follow instructions",
  "Parsing rule: wrong unless yes/no appears at the start of output",
  "GPT-4V refusals count as wrong",
  "No decoding settings, model versions or run counts given; unlikely to be reproducible exactly",
  "Images partly from public datasets (COCO etc.) though annotations are new, so image-level contamination is possible",
  "Models are 2023-era; GPT-4V is the only frontier model",
  "Suggests CoT prompting may help but does not test it"
 ],
